<title>FRANCE: ALPINE SKIING-MEN'S DOWNHILL DELAYED.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-MEN'S DOWNHILL DELAYED.</headline>
<dateline>VAL D'ISERE, France 1996-12-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The first men's downhill of the World Cup season in Europe was delayed on Saturday because of poor visitbility at the top of the piste.</p>
<p>The race, scheduled to start at 0930 GMT would  now begin at 1200 GMT, organsiers said.</p>
<p>A women's giant slalom which should have taken place here on Friday was called off because of heavy snow and will be rescheduled.</p>
<p>Bad weather also hit the start of the season in north America. The first scheduled men's downhill at Whistler, Canada last week had to be postponed.</p>
</text>
